  ],
  "sessions": [],
  "quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "I'm on a mission to solve knowledge representation when all context matters.",
      "timestamp_sec": 3,
      "talk_slug": "when-all-context-matters-extended-cache-augmented-generation",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XovaGv4f39A&t=3s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "Inserting to a vector database, it's relatively fast. So, whenever a collection becomes obsolete, we can just replace it with a new one.",
      "timestamp_sec": 51,
      "talk_slug": "when-all-context-matters-extended-cache-augmented-generation",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XovaGv4f39A&t=51s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "All the documents in the collection are relevant for us to answer the question. So, we can't just take all the documents in the collection and pass them to LLM.",
      "timestamp_sec": 93,
      "talk_slug": "when-all-context-matters-extended-cache-augmented-generation",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XovaGv4f39A&t=93s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "If your collection of documents isn't changed very often, GraphRAG is an excellent approach for finding those relationships within details to answer the user's question.",
      "timestamp_sec": 144,
      "talk_slug": "when-all-context-matters-extended-cache-augmented-generation",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XovaGv4f39A&t=144s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "Recomputing a knowledge graph every time the data gets replaced is computationally very expensive, and it takes relatively long time.",
      "timestamp_sec": 144,
      "talk_slug": "when-all-context-matters-extended-cache-augmented-generation",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XovaGv4f39A&t=144s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "where we use a model with a large context window, load the documents into the context, and cache the context by storing the model's KB matrix",
      "timestamp_sec": 192,
      "talk_slug": "when-all-context-matters-extended-cache-augmented-generation",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XovaGv4f39A&t=192s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "The problem here is that the context window is limited, and if you fill the context window too much, the quality of the answer gets degraded, too.",
      "timestamp_sec": 192,
      "talk_slug": "when-all-context-matters-extended-cache-augmented-generation",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XovaGv4f39A&t=192s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "The solution: what if we use more CAGs in parallel and distribute the documents across different context buckets.",
      "timestamp_sec": 192,
      "talk_slug": "when-all-context-matters-extended-cache-augmented-generation",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XovaGv4f39A&t=192s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "Now, each cache can answer questions regarding its content. And now we just need something to ask the right questions to the right buckets.",
      "timestamp_sec": 230,
      "talk_slug": "when-all-context-matters-extended-cache-augmented-generation",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XovaGv4f39A&t=230s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "But in practice, with very dense relationship between documents, the supervisor tends to ignore domains that at first glance seem irrelevant.",
      "timestamp_sec": 230,
      "talk_slug": "when-all-context-matters-extended-cache-augmented-generation",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XovaGv4f39A&t=230s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "For this reason, all documents are distributed in no particular order. The only requirement is to balance the number of documents in a way that the least amount of documents are needed.",
      "timestamp_sec": 230,
      "talk_slug": "when-all-context-matters-extended-cache-augmented-generation",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XovaGv4f39A&t=230s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "Then the supervisor model start exploring the buckets and progressively builds its internal understanding. And if it finds something interesting, it can ask a specific bucket follow-up questions.",
      "timestamp_sec": 277,
      "talk_slug": "when-all-context-matters-extended-cache-augmented-generation",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XovaGv4f39A&t=277s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "Because all caches can be loaded in parallel, the knowledge building process is significantly faster than graph rag while providing more accurate answers than a simple rag.",
      "timestamp_sec": 277,
      "talk_slug": "when-all-context-matters-extended-cache-augmented-generation",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XovaGv4f39A&t=277s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "And you're probably thinking, \"KV cache can be pretty expensive.\" And you're absolutely right. But there are ways to reduce that cost by optimizing how long each cache lives.",
      "timestamp_sec": 277,
      "talk_slug": "when-all-context-matters-extended-cache-augmented-generation",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XovaGv4f39A&t=277s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "And at the end, there are many retrieval strategies, and all of them have their trade-offs, whether it's compute, cost, speed. Currently, there is no one-solution-fits-all.",
      "timestamp_sec": 277,
      "talk_slug": "when-all-context-matters-extended-cache-augmented-generation",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XovaGv4f39A&t=277s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    }
  ],
  "positions": [
    {
      "claim": "Similarity-based vector RAG is unsuitable when every document in the collection is relevant to the question, because thresholded retrieval cannot return the whole collection.",
      "confidence": "stated",
      "timestamp_sec": 93,
      "talk_slug": "when-all-context-matters-extended-cache-augmented-generation",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XovaGv4f39A&t=93s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "claim": "GraphRAG is an excellent choice specifically when the document collection changes infrequently.",
      "confidence": "stated",
      "timestamp_sec": 144,
      "talk_slug": "when-all-context-matters-extended-cache-augmented-generation",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XovaGv4f39A&t=144s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "claim": "Recomputing a knowledge graph on every data replacement is computationally expensive and slow enough to disqualify GraphRAG for frequently replaced corpora.",
      "confidence": "stated",
      "timestamp_sec": 144,
      "talk_slug": "when-all-context-matters-extended-cache-augmented-generation",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XovaGv4f39A&t=144s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "claim": "Since GraphRAG already pushes every document through an LLM for entity and relationship extraction, loading the documents directly into context is not a meaningfully larger cost.",
      "confidence": "implied",
      "timestamp_sec": 192,
      "talk_slug": "when-all-context-matters-extended-cache-augmented-generation",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XovaGv4f39A&t=192s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "claim": "Filling a context window too full degrades answer quality, independent of hitting the hard token limit.",
      "confidence": "stated",
      "timestamp_sec": 192,
      "talk_slug": "when-all-context-matters-extended-cache-augmented-generation",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XovaGv4f39A&t=192s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "claim": "Organizing documents into buckets by domain hurts recall, because the supervisor model skips domains that seem irrelevant at first glance when relationships between documents are dense.",
      "confidence": "stated",
      "timestamp_sec": 230,
      "talk_slug": "when-all-context-matters-extended-cache-augmented-generation",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XovaGv4f39A&t=230s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "claim": "Documents should be distributed across caches in no particular order, balanced only so that the fewest documents per bucket are needed.",
      "confidence": "stated",
      "timestamp_sec": 230,
      "talk_slug": "when-all-context-matters-extended-cache-augmented-generation",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XovaGv4f39A&t=230s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "claim": "Parallel cache loading makes this approach significantly faster than GraphRAG at knowledge building and more accurate than simple RAG at answering.",
      "confidence": "stated",
      "timestamp_sec": 277,
      "talk_slug": "when-all-context-matters-extended-cache-augmented-generation",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XovaGv4f39A&t=277s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "claim": "KV cache expense can be materially reduced by optimizing cache lifetime.",
      "confidence": "stated",
      "timestamp_sec": 277,
      "talk_slug": "when-all-context-matters-extended-cache-augmented-generation",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XovaGv4f39A&t=277s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "claim": "No single retrieval strategy fits all cases; the choice is a tradeoff among compute, cost, and speed.",
      "confidence": "stated",
      "timestamp_sec": 277,
      "talk_slug": "when-all-context-matters-extended-cache-augmented-generation",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XovaGv4f39A&t=277s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    }
  ],
